def two_sum(nums, target):
    seen = {}
    for i, x in enumerate(nums):
        need = target - x
        if need in seen:
            return (seen[need], i)
        seen[x] = i
    return None

Expected O(n) time and O(n) space. Hash-table operations are average O(1), not guaranteed worst-case O(1). Checking before insertion prevents reusing an element. Tests: [], [3,3], negatives, no pair.

def find_seats(rows, k):
    if k <= 0:
        raise ValueError("k must be positive")
    for r, row in enumerate(rows):
        run = 0
        for c, seat in enumerate(row):
            run = run + 1 if seat == 0 else 0
            if run == k:
                return (r, c - k + 1)
    return None

O(total seats) time, O(1) extra space. Test empty rows, k greater than row length, runs ending at last seat, all occupied, and invalid k.
